  "content": {
    "title": "What channel is the NCAA championship on? How to watch Michigan today",
    "text": "April 6, 2026, 2:15 p.m. ETThe Michigan Wolverines and Connecticut Huskies will cap the 2026 NCAA Men's Basketball Tournament Monday night, April 6, at Indianapolis' the Lucas Oil Stadium.For those tuning in from home, the game will be broadcast at 8:50 p.m. live on TBS, TNT and truTV, and available to stream on HBO Max and Sling TV, according to the NCAA official website.The game could end with Wolverines' second national championship. In 1989, Michigan beat Seton Hall at the Kingdome in Seattle, Washington.For the Huskies, this would be their third national championship under head coach Dan Hurley.What time is the UM basketball game Monday?The Huskies-Wolverines basketball game is set for 8:50 p.m. Monday, April 6.What channel is the Michigan game on Monday?The game will be broadcast live on TBS, TNT and truTV, and available to stream on HBO Max and Sling TV, according to the NCAA official website.Michigan's radio network includes WWJ-AM (950 in Detroit) as well as more than a dozen stations across Michigan.The game is available on SiriusXM Channel 84 and on Westwood One Sports.What is Michigan's record?UM is 36-3 overall. U-M lost to Duke, Wisconsin and Purdue. Michigan is 11-2 at neutral sites.UConn is 34-5 overall and 10-2 at neutral sites.Contact Sarah Moore @ smoore@lsj.comWe occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, though, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.If you purchase through our links, the USA Today Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
